## 💡 Key Business Insight

The analysis highlights a strong relationship between **customer tenure, revenue, and service consumption**.

Customers who remain with the company longer tend to generate greater revenue and expand their consumption across multiple service categories.

At the same time, **refund activity and variations in monthly charges** can provide useful signals of potential dissatisfaction earlier in the customer lifecycle.

### 💭 Central Business Takeaway

> **Long-term customer relationships drive long-term revenue.**

The findings suggest that retaining and nurturing valuable existing customers can be as important as acquiring new customers when the objective is to maximize long-term customer value.

